---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="Wire Mesh Procurement Process — RFQ to Receipt in 8 Steps" description="A step-by-step wire mesh procurement workflow: specification, RFQ, quote comparison, sampling, contract, production QC, shipping, and receipt inspection.">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-theme-primary">Wire Mesh Procurement Process</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-theme-secondary">
      From specification to receipt inspection in eight steps, with the documents and tolerances that matter at
      each stage. Typical lead time for a first order: 30–60 days including sea freight.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-6">
      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 1 — Write the specification</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          One page, millimeters only: material grade, wire diameter (mm), opening (mm or µm), roll/panel dimensions,
          edge finish, coating type & weight (g/m²), tolerance class, and the inspection standard (ASTM/ISO) that
          governs. Generate a complete RFQ with our
          <a href="/tools/inquiry-template-generator/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">inquiry template generator</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 2 — RFQ to 3–5 suppliers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Send the identical spec to factories (see the <a href="/factories/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">directory</a>)
          and, if useful, one or two traders for price discovery. Ask each to confirm: exact wire diameter tolerance,
          coating weight, production lead time, and payment terms — in writing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 3 — Normalize and compare quotes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Quotes are rarely comparable as received. Convert each to price per m² at the <em>same theoretical weight</em>
          using the <a href="/tools/fob-price-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">FOB price calculator</a>
          and <a href="/tools/woven-wire-mesh-weight-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">weight calculator</a>.
          A quote 15% below the pack usually hides thinner wire or lighter zinc.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 4 — Paid sample & verification</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Pay for samples from the top 1–2 candidates. Measure wire diameter with a micrometer, verify opening over
          10 apertures, weigh a known area against the calculator, and test coating thickness. See the
          <a href="/sourcing-guide/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">sourcing guide</a> for a checklist.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 5 — Contract & deposit</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Put tolerances, the inspection standard, packaging, late-delivery terms, and payment schedule in the
          proforma invoice / sales contract. Standard terms: 30% T/T deposit, 70% against B/L copy. Beneficiary name
          must match the company name exactly.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 6 — Production & mid-production QC</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          For orders above ~$10,000, book a third-party inspection (SGS, BV, TÜV, or a local QC agency in Shijiazhuang)
          at 30–50% production completion. They check wire diameter, opening, welding/soldering quality, coating weight,
          and dimensions against the contract. Cost: typically $200–$400 per man-day — cheap insurance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 7 — Shipping & documents</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          Confirm container loading efficiency with the
          <a href="/tools/container-loading-calculator/" class="text-theme-accent hover:underline">container loading calculator</a>
          before booking. Required documents: commercial invoice, packing list, B/L, certificate of origin
          (Form A / RCEP where applicable), and any inspection report. Check every document against the contract
          before paying the balance.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
        <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Step 8 — Receipt inspection</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary leading-relaxed">
          On arrival: count rolls/panels against the packing list, check for transit damage and moisture, spot-measure
          wire diameter and weigh sample pieces. File claims with photos within the contract claim period (usually
          30 days). Feed measured values back into your spec for the next order.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary">Typical timeline</h2>
    <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border border-theme">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-theme-card text-theme-primary">
            <th class="border border-theme px-3 py-2 text-left">Stage</th>
            <th class="border border-theme px-3 py-2 text-left">Working days</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="odd:bg-theme even:bg-theme-card"><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">Spec + RFQ</td><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">3–7</td></tr>
          <tr class="odd:bg-theme even:bg-theme-card"><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">Quote comparison & sampling</td><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">10–20</td></tr>
          <tr class="odd:bg-theme even:bg-theme-card"><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">Production</td><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">15–35</td></tr>
          <tr class="odd:bg-theme even:bg-theme-card"><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">Sea freight (Asia→EU/US)</td><td class="border border-theme px-3 py-1.5 text-theme-secondary">20–40</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-xl p-6">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-bold text-theme-primary">Want a shortcut?</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-secondary">
        <a href="/inquiry/" class="text-theme-accent font-semibold">Send us your requirement</a> and we will route it to
        verified Anping factories and help you normalize the quotes you get back.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8">
    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-theme-primary mb-4">Related Guides</h2>
    <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <a href="/blog/wire-mesh-procurement-checklist/" class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-theme-primary transition block">
          <div class="font-semibold text-theme-primary">Procurement Checklist</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-theme-secondary">28-point RFQ template</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/wire-mesh-moq-sampling/" class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-theme-primary transition block">
          <div class="font-semibold text-theme-primary">MOQ & Sampling Strategy</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-theme-secondary">Negotiate lower minimums</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/blog/how-to-verify-china-wire-mesh-factory/" class="bg-theme-card border border-theme rounded-lg p-4 hover:border-theme-primary transition block">
          <div class="font-semibold text-theme-primary">Factory Verification</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-theme-secondary">On-site & remote audits</div>
        </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
